(window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY = window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY || {})["2026-09-09"] = {"meta":{"id":"2026-09-09","label":"2026 年 9 月 9 日","date":"2026-09-09","range":"","theme":"经济","themes":["经济"],"sources":["BARRON’S"],"title":"As Billionaires’ Ranks Swell, Here’s One","titleZh":"","counts":{"article":0,"paragraph":13,"vocab":24,"question":15,"qa":3,"original":5,"layout":1},"tabs":{"articles":false,"reading":true,"tests":true,"qa":true,"originals":true}},"articles":[],"reading":[{"file":"9.9精读(1).pdf","headline":{"title":"As Billionaires’ Ranks Swell, Here’s One","titleZh":"","source":"BARRON’S","series":"考研那些事儿之经济系列"},"paragraphs":[{"index":1,"en":"How was your August? For aviation mogul Kenn Ricci, the answer must be fantastico, after his epic 70th birthday party on Italy’s Lake Como. The multi-night, black-tie affair, which per Italian media featured entertainment from Mariah Carey, John Legend, Elton John, and Kenny G, was held at the Villa d’Este in Cernobbio.","zh":"你的八月过得如何？对航空业大亨肯恩·里奇而言，答案一定是棒极了，他刚在意大利科莫湖举办了一场盛况空前的七十岁生日派对。据意大利媒体报道，这场持续多晚、要求身着黑领结礼服的盛大活动在切尔诺比奥的埃斯特庄园酒店举行，玛丽亚·凯莉、约翰·传奇、埃尔顿·约翰、肯尼·基均登台献艺。"},{"index":2,"en":"The five-star luxury hotel, formerly a noble residence from the 16th century, is a “favorite and regular stop for Ricci [pronounced ‘Ricky’]… on his many visits to Lake Como for over 30 years,” notes the website of Flexjet, the company he chairs.","zh":"由里奇担任董事长的Flexjet公司官网指出，这家五星级豪华酒店原是16世纪的一处贵族宅邸，是里奇（发音为“瑞奇”）……三十多年来频繁造访科莫湖时最钟爱、最常光顾的下榻之处。"},{"index":3,"en":"The party had locals wondering whether hosting an affair of this magnitude was too much for Lake Como. Leading up to the party, news outlet La Provencia reported that a “small army is hard at work: hundreds of professionals including artistic directors, audio/lighting technicians, set designers, drivers, makeup artists, hairstylists, and service staff. Other villas and lodging facilities have been reserved to accommodate the crew.”","zh":"这场派对的规模让当地人不禁发问：科莫湖能否承办如此规模的活动。派对筹备期间，新闻机构《拉普罗文西亚》报道称：”一大批人马正在紧锣密鼓地忙碌：数百名专业人员参与其中，包括艺术总监、音/灯光技师、舞美设计师、司机、化妆师、发型师及服务人员。另有其他别墅与住宿设施被预订，用来安置工作人员。”"},{"index":4,"en":"It’s the stuff of “Champagne wishes and caviar dreams,” as Robin Leach used to say—and some light summer fare for Barron’s readers. But Ricci’s blowout is also emblematic of the flood of wealthy Americans invading Europe (basking in the glow of the strong U.S. dollar), and the soaring business of private aviation (no doubt, many of his guests flew on Ricci’s Flexjet—a smaller, privately held competitor of Berkshire Hathaway–owned NetJets).","zh":"正如罗宾·里奇昔日所言，这是一场“香槟之愿、鱼子酱之梦”的盛事，也是《巴伦周刊》读者茶余饭后的夏日谈资。但里奇这场狂欢派对同时也是两种潮流的缩影：一是美国富人涌入欧洲（享受美元走强带来的购买力红利），二是私人航空业务的蓬勃发展（毫无疑问，他的许多宾客正是乘坐里奇的Flexjet抵达现场——Flexjet是一家规模较小、私人所有的公司，也是伯克希尔·哈撒韦旗下NetJets的竞争对手）。"},{"index":5,"en":"Most significantly, though, Ricci’s soiree reflects the unfettered, inexorable rise of the ultra rich, a point brought home in a new report, Billionaire Census 2026, by research firm Altrata. The study calculated that the number of billionaires around the globe climbed 8.2% in 2025 to 3,795, the biggest increase in five years. As for their wealth, that was up a brisk 12.8% to a record $15.1 trillion, equal to 20% of the market cap of the S&amp;P 500 index, the third consecutive year of accelerating growth.","zh":"然而更重要的是，里奇的这场聚会折射出超级富豪阶层无拘无束、不可阻挡的崛起之势，这也在研究机构Altrata最新发布的《2026亿万富豪普查》报告中得到了印证。该报告测算，2025年全球亿万富豪人数攀升8.2%至3,795人，创下五年来最大增幅。其财富总额则强劲增长12.8%至历史新高15.1万亿美元，相当于标普500指数总市值的20%，这已是连续第三年加速增长。"},{"index":6,"en":"The main driver, of course, was the U.S. tech business. Ball don’t lie. The number of billionaires in the U.S., home to a third of the world’s “billies,” grew 11.5%, to 1,265. They’re worth $6.7 trillion, or 44% of global billionaire wealth. Yes, China’s billionaire population climbed 13%, but the U.S. still has three times more.","zh":"主要驱动力当然是美国科技行业。数据不会说谎。美国拥有的亿万富豪数量占全球总数的三分之一，其人数增长了11.5%，达到1,265位，财富总额高达6.7万亿美元，占全球亿万富豪财富的44%。诚然，中国的亿万富豪人数也攀升了13%，但美国人数仍为中国的三倍之多。"},{"index":7,"en":"Then there’s the very top of the food chain. “The planet’s 29 richest people, each with fortunes above $50 billion, had a combined net worth of $4.1 trillion, or a staggering 27% of all billionaire wealth,” Altrata","zh":"再来看看食物链最顶端。Altrata指出：“全球最富有的29位富豪，个个身家超过500亿美元，合计净资产达4.1万亿美元，占全球亿万富豪财富的27%，这一比例令人震惊。”"},{"index":8,"en":"This domain is dominated by U.S. tech bros. According to the Bloomberg Billionaire List, the nine richest people on the planet are all","zh":"这一领域由美国科技圈大佬主导。根据彭博亿万富豪榜，全球最富有的九人皆为美国科技界的男性“百亿富翁”（身价超千亿美元），合计身家超过2.6万亿美元。"},{"index":9,"en":"As for metropolises, don’t tell Zohran Mamdani, but New York is the leading city for billionaires, with that population rising 8% last year to 164. New York has more billionaires than any country other than Germany, China, and of course, the U.S. San Francisco comes in at No.3,","zh":"说到城市排名，先别告诉佐赫兰·马姆达尼，但纽约确实稳坐亿万富豪城市榜的头把交椅，其人数去年增长了8%，达到164位。除德国、中国以及美国本国以外，纽约的亿万富豪数量超过世界上任何一个国家。旧金山以99位富豪名列第三。"},{"index":10,"en":"The No.2 and No.4 cities, Hong Kong and London, respectively, were the only top 15 municipalities whose billionaire population fell. One could argue both are retreating from globalism—in London’s case, postBrexit, and in Hong Kong’s, the Chinese government’s economic and societal crackdown. Singapore’s billionaire population grew the most last year, perhaps at Hong Kong’s expense.","zh":"排名第二和第四的城市：香港与伦敦，是前15强城市中仅有的两座亿万富豪人数下滑的城市。可以这样解释：两者都正在与全球化渐行渐远。伦敦的原因是英国脱欧后的效应，香港则是中国政府在经济与社会层面的整顿。新加坡去年亿万富豪人数增幅最大，可能正是香港富豪流失的受益者。"},{"index":11,"en":"But back to the pride of Cleveland, Ricci, who didn’t make his fortune via today’s typical wealth-creating acronyms (GPUs or AI). Ricci got super rich the old-fashioned way, he earned it (as John Houseman said in Smith Barney ads of yore), serving the super rich; specifically, selling them fractional shares of private jets. Flexjet doesn’t release financials beyond saying it did $4.6 billion in combined 2025 year-end revenue—up from zero when it was founded in 1995. Last year, privateequity group L Catterton, which is backed by LVMH, led an $800 million investment in Flexjet.","zh":"话题转回这位克里夫兰的骄傲——里奇。他的财富并非通过当下流行的财富代名词（如GPU或AI）积累。里奇以最老派的方式成为超级富豪，他靠自己的双手赚来的（正如约翰·豪斯曼在昔日史密巴尼广告中所言），服务于超级富豪；具体而言，就是向他们出售私人飞机的“分时产权”份额。Flexjet并未公开详细财务数据，仅披露其2025年合并年终营收达46亿美元——始于1995年创立之初的零起步。去年，由LVMH支持的私募股权集团LCatterton领投了一轮对Flexjet的8亿美元投资。"},{"index":12,"en":"including $500 from his dad, and bought a small charter business. He flew musical acts like Barbra Streisand and Elton John, and became Bill Clinton’s pilot on his run for president in 1992. Ricci would later partner with Raytheon Technologies (now RTX), and then buy Flexjet from Bombardier.","zh":"里奇的故事是一段“插上翅膀的霍雷肖·阿尔杰式传奇”。他家境并不宽裕，从空军退役后成为飞行员。里奇四处借钱（其中包括父亲借给他的500美元）买下了一家小型包机公司。他曾为芭芭拉·史翠珊和埃尔顿·约翰等音乐人执飞，并于1992年成为比尔·克林顿竞选总统期间的专属飞行员。里奇后来与雷神技术公司（现RTX）合作，并从庞巴迪手中收购了Flexjet。"},{"index":13,"en":"“We’ve chosen as a family not to disguise and not to hide from our wealth,” he said recently in “How Kenn Ricci Went From Pilot to Billionaire,” the first episode of The WSJ Money Interview. “We have family meetings every quarter, and we’re passing on wealth. I’m not waiting till I die. I want to watch my kids enjoy their wealth. We have a family limited partnership the kids can borrow from to start businesses.”","zh":"“我们全家已经做出了选择，既不刻意包装财富，也不刻意隐藏财富，”他最近在《华尔街日报》金钱访谈栏目的首期节目《肯恩·里奇：从飞行员到亿万富豪》中说道。“我们每季度召开家族会议，正在把财富传给下一代。我不会等到离世才去安排。我想亲眼看着孩子们享受财富。我们设立了家族有限合伙企业，孩子们可以从中借款创业。”"}],"vocab":[{"term":"mogul","head":"n. A person who has a lot of power or money in a particular industry or activity.","definition":"A person who has a lot of power or money in a particular industry or activity.","gloss":"大亨，巨头","example":"The media mogul owns several television networks.","exampleZh":"这位传媒大亨拥有数家电视网络。","tags":[]},{"term":"epic","head":"a. dj. Something that is impressive or ambitious in size, scope or grandeur. （","definition":"dj. Something that is impressive or ambitious in size, scope or grandeur. （","gloss":"宏大的，史诗级的本义为史诗；叙事诗）","example":"The concert was an epic celebration of the band’s career.","exampleZh":"这场演唱会是对该乐队生涯的史诗级致敬。","tags":[]},{"term":"residence","head":"n. A house or other dwelling place; the fact of living in a particular place.","definition":"A house or other dwelling place; the fact of living in a particular place.","gloss":"住所，宅邸","example":"The ambassador’s official residence is in the capital.","exampleZh":"大使的官邸位于首都。","tags":[]},{"term":"magnitude","head":"n. The great size, extent or importance of something.","definition":"The great size, extent or importance of something.","gloss":"规模，量级（本义为巨大；重要性）","example":"The earthquake was of unexpected magnitude.","exampleZh":"这次地震的规模出乎意料。","tags":[]},{"term":"emblematic","head":"a. dj. Serving as a symbol of a particular quality or concept; representative.","definition":"dj. Serving as a symbol of a particular quality or concept; representative.","gloss":"象征性的，典型的","example":"The incident is emblematic of the broader crisis.","exampleZh":"这一事件是更广泛危机的缩影。","tags":[]},{"term":"bask","head":"v. To enjoy or take great pleasure in a warm or pleasant situation.","definition":"To enjoy or take great pleasure in a warm or pleasant situation.","gloss":"沉浸，享受（常与 in 连用，本义为晒太阳）","example":"She basked in the praise of her colleagues. lavish celebration or","exampleZh":"她沉浸在同事们的赞誉之中。","tags":[]},{"term":"blowout","head":"n. A large, party; an easy victory.","definition":"A large, party; an easy victory.","gloss":"盛大派对；轻松取胜（本义为爆胎；井喷）","example":"They threw a blowout for their daughter’s graduation.","exampleZh":"他们为女儿的毕业办了一场盛大派对。","tags":[]},{"term":"inexorable","head":"a. dj. Continuing without any possibility of being stopped or prevented.","definition":"dj. Continuing without any possibility of being stopped or prevented.","gloss":"不可阻挡的，坚定不移的","example":"The inexorable march of technology reshapes every industry.","exampleZh":"技术不可阻挡的步伐重塑着每个行业。","tags":[]},{"term":"brisk","head":"a. dj. Active, fast and energetic; sharp and decisive.","definition":"dj. Active, fast and energetic; sharp and decisive.","gloss":"强劲的，活泼的（本义为\"轻盈敏捷的\"）","example":"The company reported brisk sales growth in the second quarter.","exampleZh":"公司第二季度销售增长强劲。","tags":[]},{"term":"census","head":"n. An official count or survey of a population, typically recording various details.","definition":"An official count or survey of a population, typically recording various details.","gloss":"普 查 ，人口调查","example":"The national census is taken every ten years.","exampleZh":"全国人口普查每十年进行一次。","tags":[]},{"term":"driver","head":"n. A factor that causes something to happen or change.","definition":"A factor that causes something to happen or change.","gloss":"驱动因素（熟词僻义，常见义为司机；驱动程序）","example":"Consumer spending is the main driver of economic growth.","exampleZh":"消费支出是经济增长的主要驱动力。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"staggering","head":"a. dj. So shocking, surprising or extreme that one cannot believe it.","definition":"dj. So shocking, surprising or extreme that one cannot believe it.","gloss":"令人震惊的，惊人的","example":"The project was completed at a staggering cost.","exampleZh":"该项目以惊人的造价完工。","tags":[]},{"term":"combined","head":"a. dj. /kəmˈbaɪnd/ Formed by joining together; united; considered together as a whole.","definition":"dj. /kəmˈbaɪnd/ Formed by joining together; united; considered together as a whole.","gloss":"合并的，总计的","example":"The combined efforts of the volunteers saved lives.","exampleZh":"志愿者们齐心协力的努力挽救了生命。","tags":[]},{"term":"dominate","head":"v. To have a commanding influence or power over; to be the most important part of.","definition":"To have a commanding influence or power over; to be the most important part of.","gloss":"支配，主导","example":"Large corporations dominate the global market.","exampleZh":"大企业主导着全球市场。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"collectively","head":"a. dv. As a group; together; in a combined manner.","definition":"dv. As a group; together; in a combined manner.","gloss":"共同地，集体地","example":"The members collectively decided to postpone the meeting.","exampleZh":"成员们集体决定推迟会议。","tags":[]},{"term":"metropolis","head":"n. A very large and important city, especially the capital or chief city of a country or region.","definition":"A very large and important city, especially the capital or chief city of a country or region.","gloss":"大都市，首府","example":"Tokyo is the largest metropolis in Japan.","exampleZh":"东京是日本最大的都市。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"respectively","head":"a. dv. Used to show that items already mentioned are in the same order as the items just listed.","definition":"dv. Used to show that items already mentioned are in the same order as the items just listed.","gloss":"分别地","example":"Mary and Jane, respectively, won the first and second prizes.","exampleZh":"玛丽和简分别获得第一和第二名。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"retreat","head":"v. To move away from a place or enemy; to withdraw.","definition":"To move away from a place or enemy; to withdraw.","gloss":"撤退，退缩（熟词僻义，名词义为\"静修所\"）","example":"The army retreated from the battlefield under heavy fire.","exampleZh":"部队在猛烈炮火下撤出战场。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"typical","head":"a. dj. Having the distinctive qualities of a particular type of person or thing.","definition":"dj. Having the distinctive qualities of a particular type of person or thing.","gloss":"典型的，代表性的","example":"This is a typical example of bureaucratic inefficiency.","exampleZh":"这是官僚主义低效的典型例子。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"fractional","head":"a. dj. Being a fraction or small part of a whole; not whole.","definition":"dj. Being a fraction or small part of a whole; not whole.","gloss":"零碎的，分数的","example":"He bought a fractional share of the racehorse.","exampleZh":"他购 入了这匹赛马的一份份额。","tags":[]},{"term":"modest","head":"a. dj. Not large in amount, size or value; humble and unpretentious.","definition":"dj. Not large in amount, size or value; humble and unpretentious.","gloss":"不多的，谦逊的【考研大纲词汇】","example":"She earned a modest salary but enjoyed her work.","exampleZh":"她薪水不多，但乐在其中。","tags":["考 研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"charter","head":"a. dj. Hired or rented for private or special use, typically by a group.","definition":"dj. Hired or rented for private or special use, typically by a group.","gloss":"包租的，特许的（名词义为宪章；特许状）","example":"They booked a charter flight to the island.","exampleZh":"他们预订了一班包机前往该岛。","tags":[]},{"term":"disguise","head":"v. To change the appearance of something so that it looks like something else; to hide one’s true feelings.","definition":"To change the appearance of something so that it looks like something else; to hide one’s true feelings.","gloss":"伪 装 ， 掩 饰 （ 名 词 义 为 伪 装 物 ）","example":"She tried to disguise her disappointment with a smile.","exampleZh":"她试图用微笑掩饰自己的失望。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"episode","head":"n. An event or a short period of time that is different from or important in a larger sequence.","definition":"An event or a short period of time that is different from or important in a larger sequence.","gloss":"一集，一段经历","example":"The pilot episode of the series aired last night.","exampleZh":"该剧的首播集已于昨晚播出。","tags":[]}]}],"tests":[{"file":"【福利】9.9 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","type":"reading","instructions":[],"passage":[],"items":[{"number":21,"stem":"The author mentions Kenn Ricci's 70th birthday party in the opening paragraphs in order to show that _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Lake Como has become too poor to host large private events"},{"key":"B","text":"his lavish celebration reflects a broader surge of ultra-rich spending in Europe"},{"key":"C","text":"European hotels no longer attract wealthy visitors from the United States"},{"key":"D","text":"private aviation has replaced all other forms of luxury travel"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】例证题·开篇案例功能","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 1-4","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：How was your August? For aviation mogul Kenn Ricci, the answer must be fantastico, after his epic 70th birthday party on Italy's Lake Como.","- 原文（Para.3）：The party had locals wondering whether hosting an affair of this magnitude was too much for Lake Como.","- 原文（Para.4）：But Ricci's blowout is also emblematic of the flood of wealthy Americans invading Europe...and the soaring business of private aviation...","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：因果错位陷阱。当地人是质疑活动规模是否太大，不是说明 Lake Como 穷到无法承接私人活动。","- 选项B（正确）：作者用 Ricci 的奢华派对作为 emblematic example，指向富裕美国人涌入欧洲、强美元背景和私人航空业务繁荣。","- 选项C（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。原文说美国富人 flood into Europe，五星级酒店正是举办地。","- 选项D（错误）：过度推理陷阱。私人航空业务强劲，但没有说它取代所有其他奢侈旅行方式。","【命题技巧】","- 个案到群体：Ricci's blowout is emblematic 是例证题的显性信号。","- 细节与功能区分：明星阵容是例子细节，服务富豪消费趋势。"]},{"number":22,"stem":"Which of the following is true about the findings of the Billionaire Census 2026 in Paragraphs 5 to 7?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Global billionaire numbers fell to 3,795 after five years of decline"},{"key":"B","text":"China has three times more billionaires than the United States"},{"key":"C","text":"The number of billionaires rose 8.2% to 3,795, while their wealth rose 12.8% to $15.1tn"},{"key":"D","text":"The 29 richest people control 44% of all billionaire wealth"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·数据正误判断","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 5-7","【解析】","- 原文（Para.5）：...the number of billionaires around the globe climbed 8.2% in 2025 to 3,795, the biggest increase in five years. As for their wealth, that was up a brisk 12.8% to a record $15.1 trillion...","- 原文（Para.6）：...the number of billionaires in the U.S....grew 11.5%, to 1,265...China's billionaire population climbed 13%, but the U.S. still has three times more.","- 原文（Para.7）：“The planet's 29 richest people...had a combined net worth of $4.1 trillion, or a staggering 27% of all billionaire wealth.”","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。全球亿万富翁数量上升 8.2% 至 3,795，且是五年来最大增幅。","- 选项B（错误）：反向偷换陷阱。中国增幅较高，但美国数量是中国的三倍。","- 选项C（正确）：C 项准确配对两个核心数据：人数增长 8.2% 至 3,795，财富增长 12.8% 至创纪录的 15.1 万亿美元。","- 选项D（错误）：数字偷换陷阱。最富 29 人占全部亿万富翁财富的 27%，44% 是美国亿万富翁占全球财富比例。","【命题技巧】","- 双数据配对：人数增长与财富增长必须分别核对。","- 近似数字辨析：27%、44%、13%、11.5% 都来自不同统计口径。"]},{"number":23,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraphs 9 and 10 that Hong Kong and London were unusual among the top 15 cities because their billionaire populations _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"fell, while Singapore's grew especially quickly"},{"key":"B","text":"rose because both cities retreated from globalism"},{"key":"C","text":"overtook New York after 8% growth last year"},{"key":"D","text":"remained unchanged despite Singapore's rapid growth"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"[A]","analysis":["【题型】推理判断题·城市数据推理","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 9-10","【解析】","- 原文（Para.9）：New York is the leading city for billionaires, with that population rising 8% last year to 164...San Francisco comes in at No.3, with 99.","- 原文（Para.10）：The No.2 and No.4 cities, Hong Kong and London, respectively, were the only top 15 municipalities whose billionaire population fell...Singapore's billionaire population grew the most last year, perhaps at Hong Kong's expense.","分析：","- 选项A（正确）：原文说 Hong Kong 和 London 是前 15 城市中仅有的亿万富翁数量下降者；同时新加坡增长最快，甚至可能受益于香港的外流。","- 选项B（错误）：因果错位陷阱。作者说两地可能 retreat from globalism，但这不是城市亿万富翁数量上升的原因，实际数量下降。","- 选项C（错误）：细节偷换陷阱。8% 增长属于 New York，且纽约仍是第一。","- 选项D（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。两地数量下降，不是保持不变。","【命题技巧】","- 唯一性限定：the only top 15 municipalities 是本题关键。","- 城市数据归属：New York、Hong Kong、London、Singapore 的变化不能互换。"]},{"number":24,"stem":"According to Paragraphs 11 to 13, Ricci's path to wealth differs from that of many current billionaires because he _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"made his fortune mainly through popular AI acronyms and GPU companies"},{"key":"B","text":"inherited a private aviation business from his father after growing up wealthy"},{"key":"C","text":"refused outside investment while building Flexjet from a small charter firm"},{"key":"D","text":"built a business serving the super rich through fractional private-jet ownership"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·人物经历识别","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 11-13","【解析】","- 原文（Para.11）：Ricci...didn't make his fortune via today's typical wealth-creating acronyms (GPUs or AI)...serving the super rich; specifically, selling them fractional shares of private jets.","- 原文（Para.12）：Growing up in modest means and beginning as a pilot out of the Air Force, Ricci borrowed money...and bought a small charter business...then buy Flexjet from Bombardier.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。原文明确说他不是通过 GPUs 或 AI 这类当代致富缩略词发财。","- 选项B（错误）：细节杂糅陷阱。他成长于 modest means，只向父亲借过钱，不是继承私人航空企业。","- 选项C（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。L Catterton 曾领投 8 亿美元投资 Flexjet，他没有拒绝外部资本。","- 选项D（正确）：Ricci 的路径是服务超级富豪，出售私人飞机分产权；从飞行员和小包机业务起步，最终建立 Flexjet。","【命题技巧】","- 新旧财富路径对照：GPU/AI 与 fractional private jets 是核心区别。","- 白手起家细节：modest means、borrowed money 与 inherited wealth 相反。"]},{"number":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Lake Como Parties: Why Local Residents Oppose All Luxury Tourism"},{"key":"B","text":"Billionaire Boom: One Aviation Mogul Reflects the Ultra-Wealthy Surge"},{"key":"C","text":"Tech Bro Rankings: Why Only Nine Men Can Ever Become Rich"},{"key":"D","text":"Strong Dollars and Weak Cities: The End of Global Private Aviation"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】主旨大意题·最佳标题","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Full text","【解析】","- 原文（标题）：As Billionaires' Ranks Swell, Here's One Living His Best Life","- 原文（Para.5）：Most significantly, though, Ricci's soiree reflects the unfettered, inexorable rise of the ultra rich...","- 原文（Para.8）：This domain is dominated by U.S. tech bros...","- 原文（Para.11）：But back to the pride of Cleveland, Ricci...Ricci got super rich the old-fashioned way...serving the super rich...","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：以偏概全陷阱。当地是否承受得起只是派对背景，文章主线是超级富豪崛起。","- 选项B（正确）：文章先以 Ricci 派对切入，再用数据说明全球亿万富翁数量和财富上升，最后回到私人航空富豪个案。B 项同时概括宏观趋势和代表人物。","- 选项C（错误）：过度推理陷阱。九位最富者属于数据例证，不是讨论只有九人能变富。","- 选项D（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。私人航空业务 soaring，强美元也推动美国富人赴欧消费。","【命题技巧】","- 宏观与个案结构：Billionaire Census 数据与 Ricci 故事互为印证。","- 标题反推法：原标题已给出核心：ranks swell 与 one living his best life。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语阅读理解大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。","如果对答案解析有疑惑，直接打开任何AI大模型（如Deepseek、Kimi等），上传该篇原文文档，然后复制粘贴对应的题目和选项，说清楚你的疑问，大模型会回应解释对应的问题。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】9.9检验题__完型填空(1).docx","type":"cloze","instructions":["Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)"],"passage":["It’s the stuff of “Champagne wishes and caviar dreams,” as Robin Leach used to say—and some light summer fare for Barron’s readers. But Ricci’s blowout is also ____【11】____ of the flood of wealthy Americans ____【12】____ Europe (basking in the glow of the strong U.S. dollar), and the soaring ____【13】____ of private aviation (no doubt, many of his guests flew on Ricci’s Flexjet—a smaller, privately held competitor of Berkshire Hathaway–owned NetJets).","Most significantly, though, Ricci’s soiree ____【14】____ the unfettered, inexorable rise of the ultra rich, a point brought home in a new ____【15】____, Billionaire Census 2026, by research firm Altrata. The study calculated that the number of billionaires around the globe climbed 8.2% in 2025 to 3,795, the biggest ____【16】____ in five years. As for their wealth, that was up a ____【17】____ 12.8% to a record $15.1 trillion, equal to 20% of the market cap of the S&P 500 index, the third consecutive year of accelerating ____【18】____.","The single biggest ____【19】____, of course, was the U.S. tech business. Ball don’t lie. The number of billionaires in the U.S., home to a third of the world’s “billies,” grew 11.5%, to 1,265. They’re ____【20】____ $6.7 trillion, or 44% of global billionaire wealth. Yes, China’s billionaire population climbed 13%, but the U.S. still has three times more."],"items":[{"number":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"indicative"},{"key":"B","text":"emblematic"},{"key":"C","text":"suggestive"},{"key":"D","text":"characteristic"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (emblematic)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·固定搭配","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] indicative（表明的）：indicative of 可通，但不如 emblematic of 强调“典型象征”。近义干扰。","[B] emblematic（象征的）：be emblematic of 表示“是……的典型象征”。正确答案。","[C] suggestive（暗示的）：程度较弱，不能说明派对是趋势的典型体现。程度差异干扰。","[D] characteristic（典型的）：多指特性，不如 emblematic 的象征义精确。近义干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"abandoning"},{"key":"B","text":"avoiding"},{"key":"C","text":"invading"},{"key":"D","text":"criticising"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (invading)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·修辞色彩","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] abandoning（离开、抛弃）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] avoiding（避开）：与 flood of wealthy Americans 的涌入矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] invading（涌入、涌入式占领）：与 flood 呼应，形象表达富裕美国人大量进入欧洲。正确答案。","[D] criticising（批评）：不是评论行为。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"business"},{"key":"B","text":"scandal"},{"key":"C","text":"regulation"},{"key":"D","text":"collapse"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (business)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·经济语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] business（业务）：the soaring business of private aviation 指私人航空业务迅速增长。正确答案。","[B] scandal（丑闻）：感情色彩不合。语义场干扰。","[C] regulation（监管）：未讨论监管变化。语义场干扰。","[D] collapse（崩溃）：与 soaring 相反。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"conceals"},{"key":"B","text":"exaggerates"},{"key":"C","text":"misreads"},{"key":"D","text":"reflects"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (reflects)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·主题关系","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第1句","【解析】","[A] conceals（掩盖）：奢华派对反而凸显富豪趋势。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] exaggerates（夸大）：可能造成观感，但核心是反映趋势。语义场干扰。","[C] misreads（误读）：派对不是误读趋势。语义场干扰。","[D] reflects（反映）：soiree reflects the rise 表示派对反映出超级富豪崛起。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"article"},{"key":"B","text":"report"},{"key":"C","text":"speech"},{"key":"D","text":"forecast"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (report)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·来源语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第1句","【解析】","[A] article（文章）：研究报告比文章更正式。近义干扰。","[B] report（报告）：a new report by research firm Altrata 指研究机构发布的新报告。正确答案。","[C] speech（演讲）：来源形式不合。语义场干扰。","[D] forecast（预测）：后文是已计算的 2025 年数据。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"decrease"},{"key":"B","text":"stability"},{"key":"C","text":"estimate"},{"key":"D","text":"increase"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (increase)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·数字趋势","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] decrease（下降）：与 climbed 8.2% 矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] stability（稳定）：不能描述数量增长。语义场干扰。","[C] estimate（估计）：数字是研究结果，不是模糊估计。语义场干扰。","[D] increase（增长）：the biggest increase in five years 表示五年来最大增幅。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"modest"},{"key":"B","text":"sluggish"},{"key":"C","text":"brisk"},{"key":"D","text":"temporary"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (brisk)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·程度语义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第3句","【解析】","[A] modest（适度的）：与 12.8% 和 record 的强增长语境不符。程度差异干扰。","[B] sluggish（缓慢的）：方向和程度都不合。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] brisk（迅速的）：a brisk 12.8% 表示快速增长的 12.8%。正确答案。","[D] temporary（暂时的）：未强调短期性。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"growth"},{"key":"B","text":"decline"},{"key":"C","text":"reform"},{"key":"D","text":"debate"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (growth)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·趋势语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第3句","【解析】","[A] growth（增长）：accelerating growth 指增长加速。正确答案。","[B] decline（下降）：与财富创纪录矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] reform（改革）：不是政策变化。语义场干扰。","[D] debate（争论）：未涉及争论。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"victim"},{"key":"B","text":"symbol"},{"key":"C","text":"cost"},{"key":"D","text":"driver"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (driver)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·因果语义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第1句","【解析】","[A] victim（受害者）：科技行业是推动者，不是受害者。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] symbol（象征）：可作为象征，但 main driver 强调原因。近义干扰。","[C] cost（成本）：不是代价。语义场干扰。","[D] driver（驱动因素）：the single biggest driver was the U.S. tech business 指最主要的推动力。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"worth"},{"key":"B","text":"owing"},{"key":"C","text":"lacking"},{"key":"D","text":"costing"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (worth)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·价值搭配","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第4句","【解析】","[A] worth（价值为）：They’re worth $6.7 trillion 表示他们身家共计 6.7 万亿美元。正确答案。","[B] owing（欠）：owe 的现在分词，语义不合。形近干扰。","[C] lacking（缺乏）：方向相反。语义场干扰。","[D] costing（花费）：不是他们花费该金额。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语完型填空大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]}],"qa":[{"file":"9.9答疑汇总(1).docx","items":[{"locator":"","sentence":"The main driver, of course, was the U.S. tech business. Ball don’t lie.","question":"","answer":"引申义：结果自己会说话，事实胜于雄辩——不用争辩，数据/成绩摆在那里。 在本文中的用法：前一句说“主要驱动力当然是美国科技行业”，紧跟着一句 \"Ball don't lie.\"，等于用一句俏皮话给前面的判断盖章：这不是我瞎说的，数字摆在这儿，不服不行。这是财经媒体里典型的美式口语化收尾，带着一点幽默的“认了吧”的语气。 9.9 para.4"},{"locator":"","sentence":"It’s the stuff of “Champagne wishes and caviar dreams,” as Robin Leach used to say—and some light summer fare for Barron’s readers.","question":"","answer":"9.9 para.5"},{"locator":"","sentence":"\"a point brought home in a new report\"","question":"","answer":""}]}],"originals":[{"kind":"reading","label":"精读","file":"9.9精读(1).pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":854570,"date":"2026-09-09","range":"","title":"As Billionaires’ Ranks Swell, Here’s One","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\9.9精读(1).pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.9 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":56354,"date":"2026-09-09","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.9 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.9检验题__完型填空(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":60585,"date":"2026-09-09","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.9检验题__完型填空(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"qa","label":"答疑","file":"9.9答疑汇总(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":15882,"date":"2026-09-09","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\9.9答疑汇总(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"layout","label":"杂志排版","file":"9.9杂志排版.pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":775418,"date":"2026-09-09","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\9.9杂志排版.pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"}]};
